Z||000000||KissMySSFiero||04-09-2001||07:59 PM||||well yesterday was a great day and a miserable day as well.  my engine started knocking.  sounds lke lifter knock.  155k miles on the engine so it was excpected.  of course it started right after i replaced the tranny mounts, engine strut, all ebrake cables, most ofmy interior was cleaned, repaired, or replaced.  this weekend i had my entire interior out.  replaced the dash, doorpanel, installed pwr mirrors, installed 98 grand prix cd player with eq, new carpet from junk yard, new looking radio surround and just got shifter trim piece on ebay.  AND NOW THE FRIGGIN ENGINE IS KNOCKING. <BR>i guess its time for a replacement soon.  the only thing that makes me wonder is it started all of a sudden,  sounded like a balpeen hammer was hitting the side of the block.  then went away for the most part.  but its still slightly there.  and there is oil. oh well im just mourning.  she was  a good one.  but bad timing.  i wanted to do a 3.4 swap but $$$ is too short right now.  all i can afford is a low milage replacement.  which isnt bad but its not a 3.4.  oh well this is gettin too long.  <BR>later <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>    <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">        <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||9
Z||000001||Black88GT||04-09-2001||08:13 PM||||3.4 "swap" is about 200 dollars more then a "low mileage" 2.8.  For 200 dollars you get about 30 more Hp and 40 lb. ft. of torque.  Thats about 1 hp per $6.60 not to mention a stronger block.  Its your call but for an extra 200 bucks I mean, I dunno it just doesn't make sense to me.  <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">  <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I>||||reg||3
Z||000002||KissMySSFiero||04-09-2001||08:51 PM||||the main problem is really time.  i dont knwo how much llonger it will be till my engine is just done.  i think i can make it a month or so.  maybe longer.  but i would have to find a 3.4 block thats in decent shape.  if i bought a 2.8 i can get one sooner and more complete(i think) from someone more reputable(fierodave maybe) person.  a 3.4 you have to have drilled  for the starter.  im still up for opinions on this.  <P>anyone have a 3.4 block sittin around?  =Þ||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||04-10-2001||01:39 AM||||I know the feeling I change the oil in my 84SE and since the fuse box markings were missing I pulled the wrong fuse for the fuel pump. Well to make a long story short ...sniff sniff... The engine fired before the oil got pumped through the system  wheeeez sniff... then I heard it bonk bonk bonk bonk I guess all 180,000 miles caught up at once and whiped a bearing sniff sniff so off to the store I go to get 3 bottles of motor up and procieded to change the oil ....again  well it quieted thing down quite a bit but the vibration is gonna rattle the car to bits in no time. Oh well I'm hoping to get another 3000 out of it so I can get to Carlisle for the fiero fest in may..... anyone got a decent engine that will go in an 84? .....cheap!||||reg||1
